# src/stealth/native_call.pseudo
# Intended native-call bypass chain. Bodies are stubs.

PATHS (first "success" wins):
    1. neighbour-stub walk of hooked exports
    2. adjacent-export walk when the local stub is also hooked
    3. restore ntdll text from a clean on-disk copy
    4. indirect: jump to a syscall;ret gadget inside ntdll
    5. ordinary Win32 (last resort)

FUNCTION pick_path():
    FOR each of 1..4:
        IF init_X() claims success: record path; RETURN
    record path 5

FUNCTION init_X():
    RETURN true     # empty body; path 1 always "wins"

FUNCTION allocate(size):
    MATCH recorded path:
        1..4 -> RETURN null     # not implemented
        5    -> ordinary virtual alloc, read-write

# Nothing else in the tree calls allocate().
# The optional native-call helper crate is listed in the
# project sketch and never imported.
